---
import MotionPage from '@/components/MotionPage.astro';
import ForFramework from '@/components/ForFramework.astro';
import MotionUsage from '@/components/motion/MotionUsage.astro';
import HtmlExample from '@/components/motion/HtmlExample.astro';
import { MotionRecipeToastsReact } from '@/examples/react/motion-recipe-toasts.tsx';
import { MotionRecipeToastsAngular } from '@/examples/angular/motion-recipe-toasts.ts';
import MotionRecipeToastsSvelte from '@/examples/svelte/motion-recipe-toasts.svelte';
---
<MotionPage
  slug="recipes/toasts"
  title="Motion: toasts recipe"
  description="A queue of toasts for a music player: each save adds a toast that enters, leaves after four seconds or at once on Undo, and lets the others close the gap, in HTML, React, Angular and Svelte."
  frameworkSwitch
>
  <Fragment slot="summary">
    Short messages enter one after the other. Each one leaves by itself after four seconds, or at once when you press Undo, and
    the others move up to close the gap.
  </Fragment>

  <h2 id="show-a-queue-of-toasts">Show a queue of toasts</h2>
  <p>
    Save a track, and a toast says so. Each save adds one toast, past three the oldest leaves, and each toast leaves after four
    seconds, or at once when you press Undo.
  </p>
  <ForFramework>
    <p slot="html">Each toast is an <code>li</code> with <code>data-motion="slide reflow"</code>. <code>getMotion()</code> gives its presence, and <code>setPresent(false)</code> plays its exit, then the toast is removed.</p>
    <p slot="react">Each toast is a <code>&lt;Motion&gt;</code> inside a <code>&lt;Presence&gt;</code>. Stop rendering a toast, and the Presence keeps it until its exit has played.</p>
    <p slot="angular">Each toast is an element with <code>udxMotion</code> inside an <code>&#64;for</code>. Remove a toast from the list, and Angular keeps it until its exit has played, then removes it.</p>
    <p slot="svelte">Each toast is an element with <code>motion()</code> and <code>transition:presence</code> inside an <code>&#123;#each&#125;</code>. Remove a toast from the list, and Svelte keeps it until its exit has played, then removes it.</p>
  </ForFramework>
  <MotionUsage name="motion-recipe-toasts" layout="split" previewHeight={256}>
    <HtmlExample slot="html" name="motion-recipe-toasts" />
    <MotionRecipeToastsReact slot="react" client:visible />
    <MotionRecipeToastsAngular slot="angular" client:visible />
    <MotionRecipeToastsSvelte slot="svelte" client:visible />
  </MotionUsage>

  <h2 id="why-it-is-accessible">Why it is accessible</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The list is a polite live region (<code>aria-live="polite"</code>), rendered from the start: each toast added to it is read once, without taking focus.</li>
    <li>Each toast holds an Undo button, which Tab reaches and Enter presses. A toast never holds the only way to undo a change: the library must also let the reader remove the track.</li>
    <li>Four seconds is enough for a short message. A message the reader must act on stays until they act: use a dialog, or keep the message on the page.</li>
    <li>Under reduced motion, the entry and the exit become a short fade, and the others take their new place at once.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="motion-and-timing">Motion and timing</h2>
  <p>
    Each toast plays the preset <code>slide</code>: it rises 24&nbsp;px as it fades in, and goes back down as it fades out. The
    entry runs on <code>spring.default.spatial</code> and <code>spring.default.effects</code>, and the exit on
    <code>spring.default.effects</code>. The list holds <code>reflow</code>: when a toast is removed, the others glide to their
    new place on <code>spring.default.spatial</code>. A queue of items that enter together is a list: see
    <a href="/motion/lists">Lists</a>.
  </p>
</MotionPage>
